"Revokes: EO 13369, January 7, 2005","quote_kind":"verbatim_note_item","quote_truncated":false,"status":"CANDIDATE_UNVERIFIED"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:13446","date":"2007-09-28","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"OFR API record executive_order_number=13446; citation 72 FR 56175; document_number 07-4906; field disposition_notes","sha256":"8ba9e1cce593bb06b6be625b585b15bb04a1555ed34ad8c5b6f8c9bd81f83f77","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRESDOCU&fields%5B%5D=citation&fields%5B%5D=disposition_notes&fields%5B%5D=document_number&fields%5B%5D=executive_order_number&fields%5B%5D=html_url&fields%5B%5D=pdf_url&fields%5B%5D=president&fields%5B%5D=publication_date&fields%5B%5D=raw_text_url&fields%5B%5D=signing_date&fields%5B%5D=title&format=json&include_pre_1994_docs=true&order=executive_order_number&page=6&per_page=1000&search_after_cursor=WzEyNDk3LjAsIjEyNDk3Il0"}},"suggested":true}],"whole_order_end_total":1},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"done_now_by_custody","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2005-01-07","later-events_catalog":"2005-01-07","research/stage21/original_sources/CASE_ORIGINAL_SOURCE_CUSTODY.csv":"2005-01-07","stage19_causal_queue":"2005-01-07","stage21_crosswalk":"2005-01-07"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:13369","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Establishment. There is established the President’s Advisory Panel \non Federal Tax Reform (Advisory Panel).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Advisory Panel shall be composed of up to \nnine members appointed by the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The President shall designate one member of the Advisory Panel to \nserve as Chair and one member to serve as Vice Chair.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Purpose. The purpose of the Advisory Panel shall be to submit \nto the Secretary of the Treasury in accordance with this order a report \nwith revenue neutral policy options for reforming the Federal Internal Rev-\nenue Code. These options should:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) simplify Federal tax laws to reduce the costs and administrative \nburdens of compliance with such laws;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) share the burdens and benefits of the Federal tax structure in an \nappropriately progressive manner while recognizing the importance \nof homeownership and charity in American society; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) promote long-run economic growth and job creation, and better en-\ncourage work effort, saving, and investment, so as to strengthen the \ncompetitiveness of the United States in the global marketplace.\nAt least one option submitted by the Advisory Panel should use the Federal \nincome tax as the base for its recommended reforms.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Department of the Treasury shall provide, \nto the extent permitted by law, administrative support and funding for \nthe Advisory Panel. The Advisory Panel is established within the Department \nof the Treasury for administrative purposes only.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Chair of the Advisory Panel shall convene and preside at the \nmeetings of the Advisory Panel, determine its agenda after consultation \nwith the Vice Chair, and direct its work. The Advisory Panel shall have \na staff headed by an Executive Director who shall be selected by the President \nand report to the Chair.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Members of the Advisory Panel shall serve without compensation \nfor their work on the Advisory Panel. Members of the Advisory Panel \nwho are not officers or employees in the executive branch, while engaged \nin the work of the Advisory Panel, may be allowed travel expenses, including \nper diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by law for persons serving \nintermittently in Government service (5 U.S.C. 5701 through 5707), consistent \nwith the availability of funds.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Consistent with applicable law, heads of executive departments and \nagencies shall provide to the Advisory Panel such assistance, including \nassignment or detail of personnel, and information as may be necessary \nfor the Advisory Panel to perform its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(d)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) The Advisory Panel may conduct meetings in appropriate locations \nthroughout the United States to obtain information and advice from Ameri-\ncans of diverse backgrounds and experience and from a diverse range of \nVerDate jul<14>2003 17:54 Jan 11, 2005 Jkt 205001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4790 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\12JAE0.SGM 12JAE0\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n2324 Federal Register / Vol. 70, No. 8 / Wednesday, January 12, 2005 / Presidential Documents \nAmerican entities, including large and small for-profit and non-profit organi-\nzations, State, local, and tribal governments, and from other individuals \nand entities as appropriate. Public hearings shall be held at the call of \nthe Chair.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(e)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) Insofar as the Federal Advisory Committee Act, as amended (5 U.S.C. \nApp.) (the ‘‘Act’’), may apply to the Advisory Panel, any functions of the \nPresident under that Act, except for those in section 6 of that Act, shall \nbe performed by the Secretary of the Treasury in accordance with the guide-\nlines that have been issued by the Administrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(f)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec4(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. Report. The Advisory Panel shall submit to the Secretary of the \nTreasury a report containing policy options in accordance with section 3 \nof this order as soon as practicable, but not later than July 31, 2005.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 5","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed to impair \nor otherwise affect the functions of the Director of the Office of Management \nand Budget relating to budget, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 6(a)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec6(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity, against the United \nStates, its departments, agencies, entities, officers, employees or agents, or \nany other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 6(b)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec6(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Termination. The Advisory Panel shall terminate 30 days after submit-\nting its report pursuant to section 5 of this order.\nW","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 2323, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 7","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13369#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (70 FR 2323)","sha256":"3f23b91227bd02f0a817e2ac9fb4babceba4057fa0298183a8c3e36f39cca439","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-01-12/pdf/05-771.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 17 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:13369"}
